I should explain here how it will work. Despite a first sketch of a 
structure, a Wiki tends to become rapidly more like a wild bush because 
people are encouraged to add pages and namespaces, and this is done 
without concertation with the other authors. I think we should no try to 
impose a given structure, but rather, let people add pages freely.

If we just keep that, the 'Index' (the left panel) as it is currently on 
the prototype Wiki will rapidly become unreadable. However, I plan to 
add a path that associates a table of content (TOC, indeed, they are 
wiki page themselve!) in replacement of the 'Index' for given 
namespaces. This will hide the complexity and lack of organization 
behind well-structured TOC. You can see a live example of this mechanism 
at: http://www.jandecaluwe.com/testwiki/doku.php/navigation:sidebar_details.

Best,

Philippe Grosjean


