Yes, me too..., but the problem is that you often cannot guess which is 
the right page without parsing R code (certainly for generic 
functions/methods, and also alternatively for the few duplicated 
functions accross packages -remeber we plan to put *all* CRAN 
documentation on the wiki-). Since R code displayed in the Wiki is not 
parsed, the best way is to display a list of all potentially interesting 
pages... hence the search result page. All this comes from the 
complexity and ambiguity of R code without parsing it!

> Another possiblity one might consider with the difficulty level stuff is to do something similar to what
